\begin{document}
\section*{Optimal-order distinct distances in every dimension at least three}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
\textit{Higher-dimensional distinct distances}: For fixed $d\ge3$, the claimed distance lower bound for $n$ distinct points in $\mathbb R^d$ is $c_d n^{2/d}$. The constant depends only on dimension, with no vanishing subpower factor.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
\textit{Higher-dimensional distinct distances}: Polynomial interpolation and Hilbert-function estimates track concentration at several degree scales. Geometry of skew-form evaluation flats gives sparse-cone and rich-motion bounds, with exceptional algebraic families treated explicitly. These incidence estimates are combined with the distance reduction in a way that retains a fixed multiplicative constant rather than only the exponent up to a small loss.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
\textit{Higher-dimensional distinct distances}: For each fixed d>=3, every n-point set in R\textasciicircum{}d has at least c\_d n\textasciicircum{}(2/d) distinct distances; no sharp planar bound is asserted.

With the hypotheses and conventions above, the claimed result addresses the whole mathematical assertion on this page.

\subsection{Formal verification}
\textit{Higher-dimensional distinct distances}: The pinned catalogue lists no Lean formalization for this result.

This site has not run the Lean development. These links describe OpenAI’s selected formal statements and should be read with their stated scope.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI reports that an internal model produced the manuscripts. Their arguments have not been independently verified as proofs by this site. Any portion outside the documented formal scope may contain mistakes, and the catalogue label reports the announced mathematical claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{The higher-dimensional Erdős distinct-distances conjecture}, 2026-09-23; citation key \texttt{OAI:The-higher-dimensional-Erdos-distinct-distances-conjecture-September-23-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-higher-dimensional-Erdos-distinct-distances-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-higher-dimensional-Erdos-distinct-distances-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-higher-dimensional-Erdos-distinct-distances-conjecture-September-23-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/The-higher-dimensional-Erdos-distinct-distances-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
\end{itemize}
\end{document}

